{
  "raw": {
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161805": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Honors College",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Honors College at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty. Instructors are responsible for leveraging their expertise to deliver education services to students through: Preparing course plans and materials Delivering courses Monitoring progress/attendance Advising students Recording grades and submitting reports Instructor with a Master’s degree in discipline with two (2) years of experience. Teaching experience preferred. This is a part-time, temporary position that may require day, evening and/or weekend availability. Only online applications will be accepted. It is not necessary to contact the campus. No phone calls or agency calls, please. All adjunct faculty positions are filled based on course availability and Departmental need.  The Hiring Department may contact qualified candidates at any time. The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is the second-largest campus in the University of Tennessee System and serves a diverse student body of more than 11,000 undergraduate and graduate students through five academic colleges. Since its founding as Chattanooga University in 1886, UTC has established a reputation for excellence built on a unique blend of the private and public traditions of American higher education. Today, UTC brings a passion for excellence in all pursuits and is dedicated to making a difference in our community and in the lives of our students. Nestled between scenic Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers breathtaking natural beauty, lively city amenities and a small-town feel. Our city has it all, with historic cultural institutions like the Chattanooga Symphony Orchestra and the Bessie Smith Cultural Center, iconic attractions like Rock City and Ruby Falls, opportunities for epic outdoor adventures, and an eclectic contemporary art, music and food scene. Chattanooga's robust economy fosters an environment where tech start-ups thrive alongside established industries and corporations. It’s where innovation meets tradition, creating endless opportunities for growth and success. UTC embodies Chattanooga’s dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city’s most vital institutions where progressive transformation and community thrive. UTC is where Chattanooga goes to build the future."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161806": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, ESL",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga Location: Chattanooga, TN  The English as a Second Lanuage Institute at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty. Instructors are responsible for leveraging their expertise to deliver education services to students through: Preparing course plans and materials Delivering courses Monitoring progress/attendance Advising students Recording grades and submitting reports Instructor with a Master’s degree is preferred; however, candidates will be considered who have an undergraduate degree plus a CELTA or other TESOL certification.  Two (2) years teaching experience in discipline is preferred.   This is a part-time, temporary position that may require day, evening and/or weekend availability. Only online applications will be accepted. It is not necessary to contact the campus. No phone calls or agency calls, please. All adjunct faculty positions are filled based on course availability and Departmental need.  The Hiring Department may contact qualified candidates at any time. The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga proudly calls Chattanooga home—a city lauded by U.S. News and World Report, Money Magazine and Southern Living (to name a few!) for its unique blend of historic charm and modern vibrancy. Nestled between scenic Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers breathtaking natural beauty, lively city amenities and a small-town feel. Our city has it all, with historic cultural institutions like the Chattanooga Symphony Orchestra and the Bessie Smith Cultural Center, iconic attractions like Rock City and Ruby Falls, opportunities for epic outdoor adventures, and an eclectic contemporary art, music and food scene. Chattanooga's robust economy fosters an environment where tech start-ups thrive alongside established industries and corporations. It’s where innovation meets tradition, creating endless opportunities for growth and success. UTC embodies Chattanooga’s dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city’s most vital institutions where progressive transformation and community thrive. UTC is where Chattanooga goes to build the future."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/188183": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor - Department of Occupational Therapy, College of Health, Education and Professional Studies",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Department of Occupational Therapy at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga (UTC) seeks a full-time 9-month, tenure track faculty member in the Doctor of Occupational Therapy (OTD) Program. Within this role, opportunities exist for maintaining some clinical practice. Effective Date: August 1, 2026 or later depending upon availability of the selected candidate. Responsibilities: Teach and advise students within the OTD Program Engage in research with regular scholarly dissemination Engage in department, college, university service and/or professional service Contribute to OT Department outcome as s essment, OTD Program accreditation activities, curriculum and other continuous quality improvement initiatives Engage in ongoing professional development in andragogy and clinical occupational therapist skills as related to teaching assignments Required qualiﬁcations: Terminal academic degree (e.g., PhD, EdD) Occupational Therapy degree Tennessee licensed or eligible American Occupational Therapy Association member 3+ years full-time clinical experience Expertise for lead teaching of research methodologies and evidenced-based practice additional program content areas related to clinical expertise additional program content areas related to evolving curricular need(s) Preferred qualiﬁcations: Experience in lead teaching at the doctoral level Experience in research with peer-reviewed product dissemination Service and leadership in the occupational therapy profession Orthopedic clinical expertise with Certified Hand Therapist (CMT), Certified Orthopedic Manual Therapist (COMT), or other specialty certiﬁcation Clinical experience in multiple healthcare settings (e.g., outpatient, acute care, home health, skilled nursing, inpatient rehab) Clinical experience with management of patients with signiﬁcant multi-system involvement Application Process: Applicants must submit the following materials electronically through the UTC Faculty Career Job Site: Letter of interest Current curriculum vitae All higher education transcripts Statement of teaching philosophy Names, titles, and email addresses for three (3) references for conﬁdential letters of recommendation to be requested Inquiries may be made to Dr. Taylor Kozell at Taylor-Kozell@utc.edu . Application review begins immediately and continues until the position is ﬁlled. The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is in the heart of one of Tennessee’s largest and most dynamic cities. As a national model for metropolitan universities, UTC collaborates with its many regional partners to offer an experiential learning environment with outstanding teaching scholars in 128 undergraduate degree programs and 55 graduate programs—at both the master's and doctoral levels. UTC and Chattanooga—nationally recognized for its downtown redevelopment and wealth of outdoor recreation—are inextricably linked, and the University is central to the workforce and economic development efforts of the region and the state. Colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business; Engineering and Computer Science; Health, Education and Professional Studies; Nursing; and the Honors College are home to an array of award-winning programs from Nursing to Computer Science, Entrepreneurship to Veteran Student Support. Innovation is a strategic focus, and UTC research and development in smart city technology is an industry leader. UTC is the first and only university in the country with access to a managed, commercial quantum computing network, and we are introducing an artificial intelligence initiative involving entities across campus and engaging partners throughout the region. From our deep ties to the city of Chattanooga to our national reputation for innovation and hands-on learning, UTC stands out as a university where students thrive, faculty inspire, and partnerships create real impact."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161773": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Marketing and Entrepreneurship",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: Rollins College of Business: Marketing and Entrepreneurship Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Department of Marketing and Entrprenuership at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga Gary W. Rollins College of Business invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty. Instructors are responsible for leveraging their expertise to deliver education services to students through: Preparing course plans and materials Delivering courses Monitoring progress/attendance Advising students Recording grades and submitting reports Instructor with a Master’s degree in discipline with five (5) years of experience. Teaching experience preferred. This is a part-time, temporary position that may require day, evening and/or weekend availability. Only online applications will be accepted. It is not necessary to contact the campus.  No phone calls or agency calls, please. All adjunct faculty positions are filled based on course availability and Departmental need.  The Hiring Department may contact qualified candidates at any time. The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is the second-largest campus in the University of Tennessee System and serves a diverse student body of more than 11,000 undergraduate and graduate students through five academic colleges. Since its founding as Chattanooga University in 1886, UTC has established a reputation for excellence built on a unique blend of the private and public traditions of American higher education. Today, UTC brings a passion for excellence in all pursuits and is dedicated to making a difference in our community and in the lives of our students. Nestled between scenic Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers breathtaking natural beauty, lively city amenities and a small-town feel. Our city has it all, with historic cultural institutions like the Chattanooga Symphony Orchestra and the Bessie Smith Cultural Center, iconic attractions like Rock City and Ruby Falls, opportunities for epic outdoor adventures, and an eclectic contemporary art, music and food scene. Chattanooga's robust economy fosters an environment where tech start-ups thrive alongside established industries and corporations. It’s where innovation meets tradition, creating endless opportunities for growth and success. UTC embodies Chattanooga’s dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city’s most vital institutions where progressive transformation and community thrive. UTC is where Chattanooga goes to build the future."
