    "https://apply.interfolio.com/181302": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Counselor Education, School of Professional Studies, College of Health, Education and Professional Studies",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: College of Health, Education and Professional Studies: School of Professional Studies: Counselor Education Location: Chattanooga, TN  The School of Professional Studies at The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga seeks applications for a full-time, tenure-track, nine-month Counselor Educator at the Assistant rank to begin in the Fall of 2027 . UTC offers CACREP-accredited M.Ed. programs in both school counseling and clinical mental health counseling. RESPONSIBILITIES: Teaching graduate courses in the CACREP core and specialty areas of the  program Engaging in an active research and scholarship agenda Supervising practicum and/or internship experiences in all specialty areas Participating in service to the university, community, and profession REQUIRED QUALIFICATIONS: Doctorate in Counselor Education from a CACREP-accredited program Membership and involvement in professional organizations such as ACA, ASCA, ACES Potential for excellence in instruction and supervision. Developed research and scholarship agenda License-eligible in the State of Tennessee PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in counseling from a CACREP-accredited program. Two years post-master’s experience working in a clinical or school setting. Licensed in either school or clinical mental health counseling. Screening of applications will begin October 1, 2026, and will continue until the position is filled. Applicants should prepare to submit the following information as a single electronic Adobe PDF file (no greater than 5 MB) in the following order within our online UTC Career Site application system for consideration. Cover letter/letter of interest, including a statement on applicant’s teaching, research, and service agenda. A current CV, including up-to-date, personal contact information (email, phone, etc.) Unofficial transcripts from all universities attended Additionally, candidates will need to include names, titles, and email addresses for three (3) references for confidential letters of recommendation to be requested. About Chattanooga: UTC is in the heart of Tennessee’s fourth-largest city, Chattanooga, located in the southeastern part of the state near the border with Georgia and at the junction of four interstate highways. Conveniently situated within just a two-hour drive from Atlanta, Nashville, Knoxville and Birmingham, Chattanooga, offers the opportunity to live and learn in an exciting and enchanting environment. Dubbed the ‘Scenic City,’ and endowed with incredible vistas and popular area attractions, the city has been recognized nationally for its downtown renaissance and a revitalized riverfront that has become the blueprint for other cities to emulate. Chattanooga achieved the first gig internet capacity in the country and today has the nation’s fastest internet service with a 100% fiber network that links every residence and business in a 600-square mile area. Recently, Chattanooga was named America’s first ever National Park City. The city is home to companies such as Unum, McKee Foods, U.S. Xpress, Volkswagen, and Amazon, and a number of tech startups attracted to its blazing fast internet and low cost-of-living. Thousands of visitors are drawn yearly to the Tennessee Aquarium, Lookout Mountain, Civil War battlefield sites, the Bessie Smith Cultural Center, the Creative Discovery Museum for Children, and the weekly Nightfall Summer Concert Series held in the heart of downtown. Chattanooga also has a long and rich history interwoven with the Civil Rights movement and Native American heritage."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/161797": {
      "title": "Adjunct Faculty, Applied Leadership and Learning",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: College of Health, Education and Professional Studies: Applied Leadership and Learning Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Department of Applied Leadership and Learning at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga College of Health, Education and Professional Studies invites applications for the position of Adjunct Faculty. Instructors are responsible for leveraging their expertise to deliver education services to students through: Preparing course plans and materials Delivering courses Monitoring progress/attendance Advising students Recording grades and submitting reports Instructor with a Doctoral degree in discipline with two (2) years of experience. Teaching experience preferred. This is a part-time, temporary position that may require day, evening and/or weekend availability. Only online applications will be accepted. It is not necessary to contact the campus. No phone calls or agency calls, please. All adjunct faculty positions are filled based on course availability and Departmental need.  The Hiring Department may contact qualified candidates at any time. The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga proudly calls Chattanooga home—a city lauded by U.S. News and World Report, Money Magazine and Southern Living (to name a few!) for its unique blend of historic charm and modern vibrancy. Nestled between scenic Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers breathtaking natural beauty, lively city amenities and a small-town feel. Our city has it all, with historic cultural institutions like the Chattanooga Symphony Orchestra and the Bessie Smith Cultural Center, iconic attractions like Rock City and Ruby Falls, opportunities for epic outdoor adventures, and an eclectic contemporary art, music and food scene. Chattanooga's robust economy fosters an environment where tech start-ups thrive alongside established industries and corporations. It’s where innovation meets tradition, creating endless opportunities for growth and success. UTC embodies Chattanooga’s dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city’s most vital institutions where progressive transformation and community thrive. UTC is where Chattanooga goes to build the future."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191127": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Data Analytics (Tenure Track) - Department of Data Analytics, Gary W. Rollins College of Business",
      "description": "Posted: Aug 11, 2026 Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: Rollins College of Business: Data Analytics Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga (UTC) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Data Analytics beginning August 2027 . Responsibilities include teaching nine credit hours per semester, conducting research leading to quality refereed journal publications and conference presentations, and providing service at the Department, College, and/or University level. The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at UTC has long-standing AACSB accreditation at the undergraduate and graduate levels, serves approximately 2,400 students, and has a highly productive, collegial faculty. Preference will be given to qualified candidates who apply before September 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Qualified applicants must possess , or complete by August 2027 , a doctoral degree in Data Analytics, Information Systems, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited business school , as well as demonstrated potential for high-quality scholarly research. Applicants should also have demonstrated teaching ability in undergraduate and/or graduate courses using a variety of instructional modalities, including online instruction. Primary teaching responsibilities are expected to include undergraduate and graduate courses in Database Management Systems, Data Warehousing, Big Data Technologies, and related data engineering topics. Experience or interest in teaching courses in Artificial Intelligence, programming, and other areas of data analytics is desirable . Applicants should submit the following information through the UTC online application system: Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness A list of names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses for three professional references Applications must be submitted electronically through the UTC Faculty Careers website. About the Rollins College of Business The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga received the largest philanthropic gift in the history of UTC from Gary W. Rollins and Kathleen Rollins of Atlanta. The $40 million gift established the Rollins College of Business as the first named college at UTC. Mr. Rollins is a graduate of the business school and Vice Chairman of Rollins, Inc., a NYSE-listed corporation whose holdings include Orkin, the world's largest pest control company. The mission of the Rollins College of Business is to provide quality educational programs that produce academically prepared and business-ready graduates for a competitive global environment. The Rollins College of Business maintains AACSB accreditation, with the Department of Accounting separately accredited by AACSB. The College serves a pproximately 2,400 undergraduate and graduate students through programs in accounting, data analytics, economics, entrepreneurship, finance, human resource management, management, marketing, and related disciplines. Students are supported through the Decosimo Success Center, which provides academic advising, experiential learning opportunities, and career development services. About the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is the second-largest institution in the University of Tennessee System, serving approximately 11,500 undergraduate and graduate students . UTC offers a broad range of undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs across its academic colleges and schools. UTC combines the opportunities of a comprehensive public university with the personalized experience of a mid-sized campus. The University is committed to excellence in teaching, research, innovation, community engagement, and student success while preparing graduates to become thoughtful leaders and professionals. About Chattanooga, Tennessee The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga proudly calls Chattanooga home—a city recognized nationally for its quality of life, entrepreneurial spirit, outdoor recreation, and vibrant downtown. Nestled between Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers exceptional opportunities for hiking, climbing, cycling, paddling, and other outdoor activities while also providing a thriving arts, music, restaurant, and technology community. Chattanooga's diverse economy includes advanced manufacturing, logistics , healthcare, financial services, and a rapidly growing technology sector, creating outstanding opportunities for collaboration, applied research, and student engagement. UTC embodies Chattanooga's dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city's most important institutions for education, innovation, and community impact. Additional information about the Gary W. Rollins College of Business and the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga can be found at: https://www.utc.edu/rollins-college-of-business https://www.utc.edu/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/191133": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Logistics and Supply Chain Management (Tenure Track) - Department of Data Analytics, Gary W. Rollins College of Business",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: Rollins College of Business: Data Analytics Location: Chattanooga, TN  The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga (UTC) invites applications for a tenure-track faculty position in Logistics and Supply Chain Management beginning August 2027 . Responsibilities include teaching nine credit hours per semester, conducting research leading to quality-refereed journal publications and conference presentations, and providing service at the d epartment, c ollege, and/or u niversity level. The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at UTC has long-standing AACSB accreditation at the undergraduate and graduate levels, serves approximately 2,400 students, and has a highly productive, collegial faculty. This position will support the Department of Data Analytics and its newly established Bachelor of Science in Business Administration (BSBA) in Logistics and Supply Chain Management. The successful candidate will contribute to the continued growth of the program through excellence in teaching, scholarship, and service. Preference will be given to qualified candidates who apply before September 15, 2026. Applications will continue to be accepted until the position is filled. Qualified applicants must possess , or complete by August 2027 , a doctoral degree in Logistics, Supply Chain Management, Operations Management, Industrial Engineering, Business Analytics, or a closely related field from an AACSB-accredited business school , as well as demonstrated potential for high-quality scholarly research. Applicants should also have demonstrated teaching ability in undergraduate and/or graduate courses using a variety of instructional modalities, including online instruction. Primary teaching responsibilities are expected to include undergraduate and graduate courses in logistics , supply chain management, transportation, operations management, procurement, inventory management, global supply chains, and related areas. Experience or interest in teaching courses involving data analytics, artificial intelligence, optimization, business intelligence, or related analytical methods applied to supply chain management is desirable. Applicants should submit the following information through the UTC online application system: Cover Letter / Letter of Interest Curriculum Vitae Evidence of teaching effectiveness A list of names, addresses, telephone numbers, and email addresses for three professional references Applications must be submitted electronically through the UTC Faculty Careers website. About the Rollins College of Business The Gary W. Rollins College of Business at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga received the largest philanthropic gift in the history of UTC from Gary W. Rollins and Kathleen Rollins of Atlanta. The $40 million gift established the Rollins College of Business as the first named college at UTC. Mr. Rollins is a graduate of the business school and Vice Chairman of Rollins, Inc., a NYSE-listed corporation whose holdings include Orkin, the world's largest pest control company. The mission of the Rollins College of Business is to provide quality educational programs that produce academically prepared and business-ready graduates for a competitive global environment. The Rollins College of Business maintains AACSB accreditation, with the Department of Accounting separately accredited by AACSB. The College serves appro ximately 2,400 undergraduate and graduate students t hrough programs in accounting, data analytics, economics, entrepreneurship, finance, human resource management, management, marketing, and related disciplines. Students are supported through the Decosimo Success Center, which provides academic advising, experiential learning opportunities, and career development services. About the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is the second-largest institution in the University of Tennessee System, serving approximately 11,500 undergraduate and graduate students . UTC offers a broad range of undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral programs across its academic colleges and schools. UTC combines the opportunities of a comprehensive public university with the personalized experience of a mid-sized campus. The University is committed to excellence in teaching, research, innovation, community engagement, and student success while preparing graduates to become thoughtful leaders and professionals. About Chattanooga, Tennessee The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga proudly calls Chattanooga home—a city recognized nationally for its quality of life, entrepreneurial spirit, outdoor recreation, and vibrant downtown. Nestled between Lookout Mountain and the Tennessee River, Chattanooga offers exceptional opportunities for hiking, climbing, cycling, paddling, and other outdoor activities while also providing a thriving arts, music, restaurant, and technology community. Chattanooga's diverse economy includes advanced manufacturing, logistics , healthcare, financial services, and a rapidly growing technology sector, creating outstanding opportunities for collaboration, applied research, and student engagement. UTC embodies Chattanooga's dynamic spirit, serving as one of the city's most important institutions for education, innovation, and community impact. Additional information about the Gary W. Rollins College of Business and the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga can be found at: https://www.utc.edu/rollins-college-of-business https://www.utc.edu/"
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/195380": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor, Psychiatric Mental Health - College of Nursing",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: College of Nursing Location: Chattanooga, TN  The College of Nursing at The University of Tennessee Chattanooga (UTC) seeks a full-time, 12-month faculty member for a tenure-earning position. The College of Nursing offers the BSN and DNP degrees in nursing and embraces the shared governance model and Boyer's model of scholarship. Responsibilities: Teach, advise, and engage in scholarship activities primarily in the Doctor of Nursing Practice: Psychiatric Mental Health Nurse Practitioner Program. If needed, this person may be asked to support the undergraduate Mental Health courses by teaching or overseeing clinical experiences for the traditional or accelerated BSN programs. Participate in the College of Nursing, university service, and/or professional service. Assist in monitoring and supporting learner success and collaborate with curriculum development and revision. Master's degree in psychiatric-mental h ea lth nursing as a PMHNP or FNP/AGNP with current employment in the psychiatric/mental health area, either as a clinician or faculty in a College of Nursing;  Doctor a l preparation in nur s ing or a related field. Will consider MSN if the applicant is in a doctoral program and will complete the degree within one year of employment. Clinical experience working with clients with psychiatric illness, serious m ental illness, and/or substance abuse is preferred. Academic teaching experience pref erred . Submit a letter of interest, a current curriculum vitae, copies of transcripts, and a state ment of teaching philosophy. Inquiries may be made to Dr. Christine Smith via telephone at ( 423) 425- 5766. Application re v i ew begins immedi a tel y and continues until the position is filled . Transcripts for a ll post-secondary acad emic work and three letters of professional refer e nc e are subject to b e requested of all applica nt s during the screeni ng process. About Us The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is in the heart of one of Tennessee’s largest and most dynamic cities. As a national model for metropolitan universities, UTC collaborates with its many regional partners to offer an experiential learning environment with outstanding teaching scholars in 128 undergraduate degree programs and 55 graduate programs—at both the master's and doctoral levels. UTC and Chattanooga—nationally recognized for its downtown redevelopment and wealth of outdoor recreation—are inextricably linked, and the University is central to the workforce and economic development efforts of the region and the state. Colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business; Engineering and Computer Science; Health, Education and Professional Studies; and the Honors College are home to an array of award-winning programs from Nursing to Computer Science, Entrepreneurship to Veteran Student Support. Innovation is a strategic focus, and UTC research and development in smart city technology is an industry leader. UTC is the first and only university in the country with access to a managed, commercial quantum computing network, and we are introducing an artificial intelligence initiative involving entities across campus and engaging partners throughout the region. From our deep ties to the city of Chattanooga to our national reputation for innovation and hands-on learning, UTC stands out as a university where students thrive, faculty inspire, and partnerships create real impact."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196231": {
      "title": "Dual Enrollment Instructor - M.O.C.S Start",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga Location: Chattanooga, TN  Posted: Oct 22, 2026 The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga (UTC) is seeking qualified and engaging instructors to teach college-level courses to eligible high school students through M.O.C.S. Start: UTC’s Dual Enrollment Program. This is an opportunity for educators who are passionate about their discipline, committed to student success, and energized by the opportunity to introduce high school students to the expectations and possibilities of college-level learning. Dual enrollment courses may be offered on the UTC campus, online, or at participating high school locations. POSITION RESPONSIBILITIES Dual Enrollment Instructors will: Deliver high-quality college-level instruction consistent with approved UTC course descriptions, learning outcomes, curriculum, and academic standards. Teach assigned courses with the same academic rigor and expectations applicable to comparable UTC courses. Create engaging, inclusive, and student-centered learning environments that encourage curiosity, critical thinking, and meaningful participation. Provide clear expectations, instruction, assessment, and timely feedback appropriate for college-level learners. Support students as they navigate their first college-level academic experiences. Maintain accurate course records, grades, attendance, and other required documentation. Communicate effectively with students, university personnel, and appropriate school partners. Participate in required UTC orientation, professional development, training, and program activities. Comply with UTC policies, academic standards, applicable Tennessee requirements, and SACSCOC expectations. Candidates must meet UTC faculty appointment requirements and applicable SACSCOC faculty-credential guidelines for the specific course assignment . Minimum qualifications generally include: A master’s degree or higher in the teaching discipline from a regionally accredited institution; or A master’s degree with a minimum of 18 graduate semester hours in the teaching discipline, consistent with applicable SACSCOC faculty credential guidelines for undergraduate instruction. Demonstrated academic preparation and subject-matter expertise appropriate to the course(s) assigned. Ability to provide official academic transcripts and a current curriculum vitae or résumé documenting educational preparation and relevant experience. Ability to satisfy UTC’s faculty credentialing and appointment review process prior to teaching. Successful completion of applicable university employment requirements and background screening, as required. Alternative Qualifications In disciplines where standard academic credentials do not fully represent professional expertise, other documented qualifications may be considered when permitted by applicable SACSCOC guidelines and UTC policy. Such qualifications must demonstrate the candidate’s preparation and competency to teach the assigned course and must be appropriately documented and approved through UTC’s faculty credentialing process. Credential requirements may vary by discipline and course. Meeting the minimum degree requirement does not automatically guarantee appointment; final qualification is determined through the appropriate UTC academic department and college review. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Preference may be given to candidates who demonstrate: Prior experience teaching at the college or high school level. Previous experience teaching dual enrollment or college-in-high-school courses . Experience working with high school-aged students in academic settings. Strong student engagement and communication skills. Experience using active-learning, collaborative, or innovative instructional strategies. A commitment to helping students successfully transition from secondary to postsecondary education. An understanding of the academic, developmental, and transitional needs of emerging college students. Position: Dual Enrollment Instructor Program: M.O.C.S. Start – Dual Enrollment Appointment Type: Adjunct Academic Discipline: Varied Instructional Location: UTC Campus | Online | Participating High School Applicants should submit: Current résumé or curriculum vitae Cover letter Official or unofficial academic transcripts, as permitted during the application process Documentation of relevant teaching or professional experience Any additional credentials or supporting documentation requested by the academic department Final appointment is contingent upon verification and approval of faculty qualifications for the assigned course(s). About Us The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is in the heart of one of Tennessee’s largest and most dynamic cities. As a national model for metropolitan universities, UTC collaborates with its many regional partners to offer an experiential learning environment with outstanding teaching scholars in 128 undergraduate degree programs and 55 graduate programs—at both the master's and doctoral levels. UTC and Chattanooga—nationally recognized for its downtown redevelopment and wealth of outdoor recreation—are inextricably linked, and the University is central to the workforce and economic development efforts of the region and the state. Colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business; Engineering and Computer Science; Health, Education and Professional Studies; and the Honors College are home to an array of award-winning programs from Nursing to Computer Science, Entrepreneurship to Veteran Student Support. Innovation is a strategic focus, and UTC research and development in smart city technology is an industry leader. UTC is the first and only university in the country with access to a managed, commercial quantum computing network, and we are introducing an artificial intelligence initiative involving entities across campus and engaging partners throughout the region. From our deep ties to the city of Chattanooga to our national reputation for innovation and hands-on learning, UTC stands out as a university where students thrive, faculty inspire, and partnerships create real impact."
    },
    "https://apply.interfolio.com/196228": {
      "title": "Assistant Professor of Music Education, General - Department of Music",
      "description": "Department: The University of Tennessee-Chattanooga: College of Arts & Sciences: Music Location: Chattanooga, TN  Posted: Oct 22, 2026 The Department of Music at the University of Tennessee at Chattanooga invites applicants for the tenure-track position of Assistant Professor of Music Education (General Music Specialist) , beginning August 1, 2027 . The UTC Department of Music is a vibrant community of performers, scholars, and educators committed to excellence in teaching, research, creative work, and service. It offers undergraduate degrees in Music Education, Music Therapy, Performance, and Composition, as well as the M.M. in Music Education. The successful candidate will become part of a dynamic faculty committed to fostering musical excellence, advancing innovative pedagogy, and contributing to the cultural vitality of the region and beyond. Responsibilities Primary responsibilities include teaching undergraduate and graduate courses in Music Education, including General Music Methods, Research Methods in Music Education, and/or Studies in Music Curricula. Pending the applicant’s interest and experience, additional teaching and advising responsibilities may include: Serving as Director of the Kodály Institute at UTC Teaching other undergraduate music education courses, such as Technology for Music Educators Teaching courses in foundation studies (e.g., Aural Skills, Music Theory, Music History and Literature), in accordance with the candidate’s expertise and Department needs Supervising student teachers Directing graduate research projects Advising music education majors The candidate is expected to build meaningful relationships with the local K-12 education community, offering clinics and workshops to area in-service teachers and facilitating field experiences for preservice teachers. Faculty in the Department of Music are expected to serve on department, college, and campus committees; pursue an active and ongoing agenda of scholarly or creative activity in their field; maintain memberships in regional and national professional organizations; and contribute to the Department’s recruitment and retention efforts, both at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Required Qualifications: Doctorate in Music or Music Education (PhD, DMA). ABD candidates will be considered, with completion expected by August 1, 2027. Three years of successful teaching experience in K-12 school settings. Demonstrated commitment to mentoring future music educators and fostering collaboration across the music education community . Recommended Qualifications: Five or more years of successful teaching experience in K-12 school settings, with evidence of broad and innovative approaches to curriculum and instruction. Elementary experience preferred. Experience teaching undergraduate or graduate music education courses. Experience in curriculum development and program assessment. Knowledge of and expertise in a wide variety of technology used in music education settings. Certification in Kodály (preferred), Orff, and/or Dalcroze approaches. Evidence of research activity with the potential for regional, national, or international impact. Applicants must submit the following materials: Cover letter Curriculum vitae (CV), including up-to-date personal contact information Statement of teaching philosophy and research interests Link(s) to video(s) of teaching (K-12 and/or collegiate settings), no more than 20 minutes Names, titles, and email addresses for three professional references Review of materials will begin on November 30, 2026 . About Us The University of Tennessee at Chattanooga is in the heart of one of Tennessee’s largest and most dynamic cities. As a national model for metropolitan universities, UTC collaborates with its many regional partners to offer an experiential learning environment with outstanding teaching scholars in 128 undergraduate degree programs and 55 graduate programs—at both the master's and doctoral levels. UTC and Chattanooga—nationally recognized for its downtown redevelopment and wealth of outdoor recreation—are inextricably linked, and the University is central to the workforce and economic development efforts of the region and the state. Colleges of Arts and Sciences; Business; Engineering and Computer Science; Health, Education and Professional Studies; and the Honors College are home to an array of award-winning programs from Nursing to Computer Science, Entrepreneurship to Veteran Student Support. Innovation is a strategic focus, and UTC research and development in smart city technology is an industry leader. UTC is the first and only university in the country with access to a managed, commercial quantum computing network, and we are introducing an artificial intelligence initiative involving entities across campus and engaging partners throughout the region. From our deep ties to the city of Chattanooga to our national reputation for innovation and hands-on learning, UTC stands out as a university where students thrive, faculty inspire, and partnerships create real impact."
    }
  },
